      "title": "Uncontrolled Recursion in io.undertow:undertow-core",
      "description": "Affected versions of io.undertow:undertow-core are vulnerable to Uncontrolled Recursion. Undertow does not send the expected `0 ` termination of the chunked response. This results in uncontrolled resource consumption, leaving the server side to a denial of service attack. This happens only with Java 17 TLSv1.3 scenarios.",
